WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.772 --> 00:00:06.070
Welcome to Ear Biscuits podcast,

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.490
where two lifelong friends talk
about life for a long time.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:11.660
I am Link.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:12.970
And I am Rhett.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:15.360
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.000
Link is going to be
sharing about a milestone,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.790
a family milestone.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:23.970
He got started on the family game

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.270
a little bit earlier than me.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:30.130
so one year ahead of me, he is pushing,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:34.523
or he has pushed his first
bird out of the nest.

00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:37.100
So not an empty nest yet.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.420
You know what?

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.880
I get to the empty nest before you.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.713
Yes, you do.

00:00:40.713 --> 00:00:41.700
Because I only had two kids.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.520
So I get to do the first
empty nest episode,

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:45.620
when that ever happens.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.640
If it happens.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.600
Whenever that happens.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.010
Empty nest is not guaranteed
for either one of us,

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.290
we both get two in the house-

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.240
But you just pushed one,

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.120
I mean, not really
completely out of the nest.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.820
You pushed her to college,
which is technically not...

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.210
She no longer lives at your house.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:01.043
Nope.

00:01:01.043 --> 00:01:02.803
And she's many, many hours away.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.380
And I'm still getting used to it.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.440
So yeah, I just...

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.930
I'm still gonna be processing this,

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.573
but I just wanted to share the
entire experience with you.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.300
I mean, like you said,

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:24.300
it's a milestone event for
our family, and for Lily.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:26.823
And as it turns out,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.780
there's been even more to
process than I anticipated,

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.210
and I thought it was gonna be a big deal.

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:39.020
So yeah, I'll walk you
through what it felt like,

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:42.000
and maybe you'll be a
little bit more prepared,

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.190
but I'm sure things will
be different for you.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:48.810
But if my story can help you in any way,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.257
Dad Rhett, I wanna do that for you.

00:01:52.257 --> 00:01:53.363
Oh, I'm sure you do.

00:01:54.393 --> 00:01:56.360
I mean, 'cause you didn't help me any.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.010
I mean, what is there to say?

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.630
You don't know anything.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:01.100
It's uncharted territory.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.517
It's like when I got
married, you were like,

00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:03.710
"Man, you're getting married.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.310
I can't help you with that yet."

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.125
Of course, I don't know
how much I helped you.

00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:08.223
Yeah.

00:02:08.223 --> 00:02:09.056
I should probably say it...

00:02:09.056 --> 00:02:12.080
Yeah, I don't recall getting any...

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.150
